<title>UK: Main North Sea daily crude liftings flat in March.</title>
<headline>Main North Sea daily crude liftings flat in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily crude oil loadings from the North Sea's eight main export systems should be flat in March, schedules released recently show.</p>
<p>March liftings under the programmes would average 4.82 million barrels per day (bpd), only 10,000 bpd more than in February.</p>
<p>Schedules for March liftings from Britain's Brent, Forties and Flotta and Norway's Ekofisk, Gullfaks, Oseberg, Statfjord and Troll detail 149.5 million barrels in 255.8 cargoes.</p>
<p>Loadings in February were expected to total 134.7 million barrels in 230.3 cargoes according to revised programmes.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
